y
&amp;= \red{-1}x^2 \blue{-1}x + \green{2} \\
&amp;= \red{-1}(2)^2 \blue{-1}(2) + \green{2} \\
&amp;= -4 - 2 + \green{2} \\
&amp;= -4 \\
\end{align*}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></span></p></div></div></div></div><div><div><div><p><span><span>Right, we calculated two points: </span></span><span><span><span><span><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\def\A{\red{A}}
